        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool FragmentSet::InsertFragment</definition>
        <argsstring>(data_fragment_set_t &amp;fragmentSet, data_fragment_t key)</argsstring>
        <name>InsertFragment</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classFragmentSet_1ab9205d52d6ea62686899e767129fadbc" kindref="member">data_fragment_set_t</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>fragmentSet</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="structFragmentSet_1_1data__fragment__t" kindref="compound">data_fragment_t</ref></type>
          <declname>key</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Insert fragment in fragment set.</para>
<para>If the fragment to be inserted fits entirely within an existing fragment in the fragment set, returns immediately and the fragment set is left unmodified. Else, the fragment is inserted in the fragment set and all adjacent fragments (greedy) to the point of insertion are modified according to the following steps:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>If the inserted fragment overlaps an existing fragment, the union fragment created from the two takes the place of the existing fragment in the fragment set.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>All abut fragments to the inserted fragment, including the inserted fragment, are reduced (condensed) to a single union fragment as well.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The rest of the fragments in the fragment set, that at this point are NEITHER overlapping-with NOR abut-to the inserted fragment, remain as-is. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragmentSet</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragment set to modify. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>key</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragment to insert. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the fragment was inserted successfully (and thus the fragment set was modified), or False otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>If returns True, the argument to fragmentSet is modified accordingly (see above for details). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
