      <memberdef kind="function" id="classFragmentSet_1a3ea00cef7b2335316b0f5f8c5295b310" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool FragmentSet::RemoveFragment</definition>
        <argsstring>(data_fragment_set_t &amp;fragmentSet, const data_fragment_t &amp;key)</argsstring>
        <name>RemoveFragment</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classFragmentSet_1ab9205d52d6ea62686899e767129fadbc" kindref="member">data_fragment_set_t</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>fragmentSet</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="structFragmentSet_1_1data__fragment__t" kindref="compound">data_fragment_t</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>key</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Remove fragment from fragment set.</para>
<para>If the fragment does not exist in the fragment set, returns immediately and the fragment set is left unmodified. Else, the fragment is removed from the fragment set and all directly affected fragments from the range removed are modified according to the following steps:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>If the fragment to remove fits entirely within an existing fragment, the range is removed and the existing fragment is thus split into either one or two fragments.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>All existing fragments that fit entirely within the fragment to remove, are simply removed.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Any existing fragments that overlap with the fragment to remove, are trimmed accordingly.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The rest of the fragments in the fragment set, that at this point are NOT overlapping with the fragment to remove, remain as-is. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragmentSet</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragment set to modify. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>key</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragment to remove. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the fragment was removed (and thus the fragment set was modified), or False otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>If returns True, the argument to fragmentSet is modified accordingly (see above for details). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
